# Ticket #4471 — Calendar and booking date discrepancies

Ticket #4471 merged 412 unique reports about calendar invites and booking dates not matching. Analysis found two distinct root causes, both stemming from locale handling failures.

## Problems identified

| Cause | Count | Description |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| Parser reads dates month-first; tenants write day-first | 385 | The shared parser assumes MM/DD format (US convention) but day-first locales write DD/MM. Dates are inverted: 4 July becomes 7 April, 10 March becomes 3 October. Affects all channels and most locales. |
| Form hint says MM/DD but tenant types DD/MM | 42 | The booking form shows a MM/DD hint but doesn't enforce it. Users follow their locale's convention instead, creating the same inversion as the parser bug. Specific to booking form users. |

**Total: 412 unique reports across 2 categories**

## Root cause analysis

Both issues stem from a failure to respect locale conventions when handling dates. The parser bug dominates (385 reports, 91% of merged reports), affecting users across all channels (app, email, form) in locales including en-GB, nl-NL, cs-CZ, de-DE, it-IT, da-DK, pt-PT, pl-PL, fr-FR, es-ES, en-IE, and en-US. The form hint issue is smaller (42 reports, 10% of merged reports) but shows the same root cause: the system assumes MM/DD while users in day-first locales write DD/MM.

## Next steps

Each problem type has been filed as a separate issue in the GitHub repo so the engineering team can investigate and fix them independently.

